PW HSE NSCF on the frozen SCF source committed in this directory (binary
wavefunctions, eig_occ.txt, chg.cube). Same k mesh with more target
bands; an explicit zero exx_fock_alpha is accepted like an omitted Fock term.

The charge density is standard SCF output generated with out_chg 1 12.
To regenerate the source, use the same STRU/KPT and INPUT with calculation scf,
nbands 3, out_chg 1 12, and out_wfc_pw 2.
The cube-based band references differ from the former binary-restart references
by at most 1.12e-4 eV: out_chg writes rho, while the binary restart writes rho_save.
INPUT.info retains only the seven source SCF parameters checked by hybrid NSCF.

Diagonalization accuracy for the band comparison:
The 1e-8 eV band check needs a tighter solver threshold than the former 1e-10.
With the stabilized CG update, the former threshold left a maximum band error
of 1.05e-8 eV and changed the last printed digit of one band. Set pw_diag_thr
to 1e-12 while retaining the default iteration budget of 50, stored references,
and comparison tolerance. At four MPI ranks, CG, Davidson-subspace and PPCG
then reproduce band.txt.ref exactly; their maximum eigenvalue differences from
a tighter PPCG control are below 1.86e-11 eV. Four independent solver controls
(CG, Davidson, Davidson-subspace, PPCG) at 1e-14 with a budget of 500 agree
within 2.4e-13 eV, confirming the stored band reference.
The default-budget PPCG substitution still reports an inner residual warning;
the band comparison does not establish convergence of that residual.
